{
  "_note": [
    "Reference data lifted out of ckf.hardmode.missions.json by the gui-plan.md 5.5 migration. The plugin deserialises none of it: MissionRewards.cs:264-283 declares type, note and the five slots and nothing else, and MissionRewards.cs:294-298 declares only \"missions\".",
    "byType.<type>.shipped, .roomFlags and .objectivePayments are regenerated by scripts/refresh_mission_roster.py from the CKF Data Dump CSVs.",
    "byType.<type>.displayName and .slotNote are HAND-WRITTEN. They were trailing // comments in missions.json before the strip. refresh_mission_roster.py preserves them and refuses to write rather than lose one.",
    "'objectivePayments' lists a mission's own cash reward terms. Each carries PctOfFullPayment where it could be recovered - the percentage of the full job payment (base curve at PowerLevelUnscaled x the contact term), which is the number that compares across missions. RewardQuantity is the resolved credits for the one mission it was captured on.",
    "'roomFlags' is the game's own RoomFlagTypes for the mission's stages: FullCombat means an all-out battle with no stealth route, MixedSkills/Stealth mean there is one. Both need the 'objectives' and 'flags' probes and a played session.",
    "'shipped' is reference only - the plugin never reads it. null means this type has not been generated in a captured session yet.",
    "secondaryObjectives is read-only reference: optional goals with non-cash rewards, captured as the game read them. The ObjectivePayment slot does NOT touch these - it scales cash reward rows only. Money secondary objectives stay under byType.<type>.objectivePayments, because they are percentages of the same base."
  ],
